5.text:
On the $q\mapsto -q$ invariant part
${\cal C}_{E}:y^{2}=2E-q^{2}+q^{n}$,

\begin{equation*}
{\rm rk}\,H^{1}_{+}(n)=\Big[\frac n2\Big]-1 ,
\qquad 
u_{r}(2k)=k-1=\frac n2-1,\qquad 
u_{r}(2k+1)=2k=n-1 ,
\end{equation*}
so that $u_{r}(n)=n/2-1$ and $u_{r}(n\pm1)=n\pm1-1$ is the parity
condition $n\equiv0\;(2)$.  Apart from the trivial quadratic
degeneration $n=2$ the first non–trivial even realisation is

\begin{equation*}
n_{1}=4,\qquad n_{2}=6,
\end{equation*}
$u_{r}(4)=1=4/2-1$, $u_{r}(3)=2=3-1$, $u_{r}(5)=4=5-1$, the strict
arithmetical first pair being the degenerate $n_{1}^{(0)}=2$,
$n_{2}^{(0)}=4$.  Put $k_{1}=n_{1}/2=2$ and

\begin{equation*}
\lambda_{12}= \frac{2}{n_{1}}\sqrt{\frac{n_{2}-n_{1}}{n_{1}/2}}
           =\frac{2}{4}\sqrt{\frac{6-4}{2}}=\frac12 .
\end{equation*}
On the $+$ eigenspace, up to an inessential additive constant,

\begin{equation*}
H_{1,2}(p,q)=\frac12\Big[p^{2}+q^{2}-\lambda_{12}q^{k_{1}}\Big]
          =\frac12p^{2}+\frac{1-\lambda_{12}}2q^{2}
          =\frac12p^{2}+\frac14q^{2},
\end{equation*}
i.e. up to an affine change of $q$ the ordinary harmonic oscillator
with

\begin{equation*}
\omega_{12}^{2}=1-\lambda_{12}=\frac12,\qquad 
\omega_{12}=2^{-1/2},\qquad J(E)=E/\omega_{12},
\end{equation*}
so that the real action period is energy independent on the reduced
branch.  The formal resonant modulus for the pair is

\begin{equation*}
\alpha_{*}=\frac{n_{1}-1}{n_{2}}=\frac{4-1}{6}=\frac12 ,
\end{equation*}
and on the quadratic $+$ branch the hypergeometric factor is constant.
In the mathematical normalisation $\widehat T(0)=1$,

\begin{equation*}
\widehat T_{0}(\alpha)=(1-\alpha)^{-1/2},
\end{equation*}
and on the $4,6$ reduced branch $\widehat T_{12}\equiv\omega_{12}^{-1}$.
Hence

\begin{equation*}
\widehat T_{12}(\alpha_{*})=\omega_{12}^{-1}
      =(1-\lambda_{12})^{-1/2}=(1-\alpha_{*})^{-1/2}
      =\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\tfrac12}}=\sqrt2 ,
\end{equation*}
i.e. $\widehat T_{12}(\alpha)\equiv\sqrt2$ on the resonant line,
the constant ${}_{2}F_{1}\!\left(\tfrac12,\tfrac12;1;\alpha_{*}\right)$
period of the $+$ branch.  In the usual physical $T(0)=2\pi$
normalisation $T_{\rm phys}=2\pi\widehat T$,

\begin{equation*}
T_{\rm phys}(\alpha_{*})=\frac{2\pi}{\omega_{12}}
   =\frac{2\pi}{\sqrt{1-\lambda_{12}}}=2\pi\sqrt2,
\end{equation*}
the constant $2\pi/\omega_{12}$ harmonic period of
$H_{4,6}=p^{2}/2+q^{2}/4$.  Up to the conventional $2\pi$ factor this
is the stripped normalised constant $\sqrt2$, the degenerate
arithmetical limit $n_{1}^{(0)}=2,n_{2}^{(0)}=4$,
$\alpha_{0}=1/4$ giving $\omega\equiv1$, $\widehat T\equiv1$,
$T_{\rm phys}\equiv2\pi$.  This is the $n_{1}=4,n_{2}=6$ resonant
realisation. ∎

